                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15154159" author="iveselovskiy" created="Fri, 19 Feb 2016 12:20:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/501&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/501&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15154264" author="vozerov" created="Fri, 19 Feb 2016 14:21:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;My comments:&lt;br/&gt;
1) IgfsFileInfo - you propagate &quot;modificationTime&quot;, but do not do that for &quot;accessTime&quot;. Is it normal?&lt;br/&gt;
2) It looks like constructor &quot;IgfsFileInfo(IgfsFile f, boolean evictExclude)&quot;. It is used in two places with the same pattern: IgfsFile -&amp;gt; IgfsFileInfo -&amp;gt; IgfsFileImpl. Let&apos;s remove it and simplify the chain: IgfsFile -&amp;gt; IgfsFileImpl.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15159407" author="iveselovskiy" created="Tue, 23 Feb 2016 18:50:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;1) fixed: accessTime is now propagated from the underlying file system as well as modificationTime. &lt;br/&gt;
Note however, that &lt;br/&gt;
(a) accessTime in IGFS is not handled as real access time (due to performance reasons); &lt;br/&gt;
(b) method org.apache.ignite.IgniteFileSystem#setTimes does not work with dual file systems, so the accessTime can be treated as a read-only property propagated from underlying file system.&lt;br/&gt;
2) fixed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
